{%- comment -%}
  PawLunova: the free-delivery claim, in one place.

  Every template that mentions free delivery renders this, so the claim can
  never drift from Settings → Delivery in the admin. Set
  `pln_free_delivery_threshold` to 0 when standard delivery is free on
  everything (the store's current setting: one UK zone, Standard £0.00 with no
  minimum) and every surface says so without inventing a spend threshold.

  Usage:
    {% render 'pln-delivery-claim' %}                -> "Free UK delivery"
    {% render 'pln-delivery-claim', style: 'long' %} -> "Free UK delivery, tracked"
    {% render 'pln-delivery-claim', style: 'short' %}-> "Free delivery"

  With a threshold set (say 40) the same calls append the minimum spend:
  "Free UK delivery over £40", "Free UK delivery over £40, tracked" and
  "Free delivery over £40".

  Callers that need the number itself still read the setting directly; this
  snippet exists so nobody has to write "over £[threshold]" into copy again.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign threshold = settings.pln_free_delivery_threshold | default: 0 | plus: 0

  case style
    when 'short'
      assign claim = 'Free delivery'
    else
      assign claim = 'Free UK delivery'
  endcase

  if threshold > 0
    assign claim = claim | append: ' over £' | append: threshold
  endif

  if style == 'long'
    assign claim = claim | append: ', tracked'
  endif

  echo claim
-%}
